VALUES ('e2e747e7-0aba-5a21-95bf-afd6abda0dd3'::uuid, '417bcbcf-1354-516f-96af-7bbe5897bffb'::uuid, 2, 'Evidence or Assumption?', 'The generated response contains several claims, but the reviewer cannot tell which are supported, conflicting, unsupported, uncertain or missing required evidence. The learner must split the response into claim units and classify each claim against the supplied evidence without deciding the customer outcome.', '["Polished GenAI output may create pressure to act before evidence is complete", "unclear source or review status", "authority pressure"]'::jsonb, '["May treat generated output as approved evidence", "may convert uncertainty into fact", "may diagnose or correct outside L1 authority"]'::jsonb, 'Northstar Retail is preparing a GenAI customer-support assistant that answers customer questions using approved business information. A generated response appears polished and confident, but the supplied records may show conflict with an approved source, internal-use information appearing in customer-facing output, incomplete review evidence, unclear source or review status, and deadline pressure encouraging premature use. The learner must inspect supplied records, identify workflow objects, classify evidence, recognise visible quality, evidence and boundary signals, record uncertainty, organise a safe review handoff and prepare a permitted first review action without diagnosing the technical cause, changing the response, approving the output or closing the case.', '["Completion of the previous module artifact where applicable"]'::jsonb, '["Recognise, classify, record and hand off supplied evidence."]'::jsonb, 'Use when The generated response contains several claims, but the reviewer cannot tell which are supported, conflicting, unsupported, uncertain or missing required evidence. The learner must split the response into claim units and classify each claim against the supplied evidence without deciding the customer outcome.', '{"major_concepts": "claim splitting, evidence matching, supported/conflicting/unsupported classification, exact excerpt capture, and neutral reviewer notes", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use when completing Evidence or Assumption? and producing the Evidence Classification Register within the learner''s L1 authority boundary", "reason_behind_concept": "Entry-level capability is demonstrated by accurate recognition, traceable evidence and safe escalation—not by changing, approving or diagnosing the workflow."}'::jsonb, '{"ai_support_tips": "After completing the human-first attempt, use the approved AI assistant to check missing evidence links, unclear reasoning, weak boundary wording, incomplete traceability, and revision quality; AI must not create missing evidence, make accountable decisions, bypass controls, or approve release", "module_continuity_link": "The Evidence Classification Register supplies the evidence judgements used in the response signal scan."}'::jsonb, '{"technical_concepts_learnt": "Workflow objects, evidence status, claim classification, signal tagging, traceability, handoff records, authority boundaries, and A01-to-A02 revision evidence", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Observation, classification, evidence-based reasoning, uncertainty language, reflective learning, and transfer of learning"}'::jsonb, 'The generated response contains several claims, but the reviewer cannot tell which are supported, conflicting, unsupported, uncertain or missing required evidence. The learner must split the response into claim units and classify each claim against the supplied evidence without deciding the customer outcome.', '{"items": ["Microsoft Excel", "Microsoft PowerPoint", "Adobe Acrobat Reader", "ChatGPT Enterprise"]}'::jsonb, TRUE, TRUE)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
