 make accountable decisions, bypass controls, or approve release", "module_continuity_link": "The L3 Builder Readiness and Authority Record defines the operating boundary for the independent build."}'::jsonb, '{"technical_concepts_learnt": "Acceptance criteria, prompt architecture, context filters, retrieval fallback, validation coverage, defect classification, controlled fixes, regression testing, and release-readiness evidence", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Systems thinking, requirements engineering, experimental design, root-cause reasoning within scope, evidence evaluation, and technical reporting"}'::jsonb, 'The learner is now expected to work independently in standard situations. Before building, the learner must confirm the routine decisions they may make, the patterns they must follow and the exceptions that require escalation.', '{"items": ["Microsoft Excel", "Microsoft PowerPoint", "Microsoft Word", "ChatGPT Enterprise sandbox", "Microsoft SharePoint", "Microsoft Edge"]}'::jsonb, TRUE, TRUE)
