traceability, and revision quality; AI must not create missing evidence, make accountable decisions, bypass controls, or approve release", "module_continuity_link": "The Workflow Objective and Acceptance Criteria Brief becomes the governing design and validation reference."}'::jsonb, '{"technical_concepts_learnt": "Acceptance criteria, prompt architecture, context filters, retrieval fallback, validation coverage, defect classification, controlled fixes, regression testing, and release-readiness evidence", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Systems thinking, requirements engineering, experimental design, root-cause reasoning within scope, evidence evaluation, and technical reporting"}'::jsonb, 'The business request describes a desired GenAI outcome but does not yet provide a testable workflow objective or measurable acceptance criteria. The learner must independently convert the request into a standard, bounded and testable definition.', '{"items": ["Microsoft Excel", "Microsoft PowerPoint", "Microsoft Word", "ChatGPT Enterprise sandbox", "Microsoft SharePoint", "Microsoft Edge"]}'::jsonb, TRUE, TRUE)
