ording, incomplete traceability, and revision quality; AI must not create missing evidence, make accountable decisions, bypass controls, or approve release", "module_continuity_link": "The Systemic Workflow Weakness Analysis identifies the practice gaps addressed through reviewer coaching and governance improvements."}'::jsonb, '{"technical_concepts_learnt": "Governance models, control plans, standards architecture, pattern-library metadata, cross-workflow analysis, reviewer calibration, coaching evidence, adoption metrics, and review cadence", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Organisational learning, governance design, quality assurance, systems analysis, coaching theory, change management, and strategic communication"}'::jsonb, 'Repeated defects appear across multiple workflows, suggesting systemic practice weaknesses rather than isolated errors. The learner must identify patterns, contributing conditions and organisational control gaps without relying on unsupported causal claims.', '{"items": ["Microsoft Excel", "Microsoft PowerPoint", "Microsoft Word", "Microsoft SharePoint", "ChatGPT Enterprise", "Microsoft Teams"]}'::jsonb, TRUE, TRUE)
